A||||6||David Gamache||seeking info on building a V-6 stroker motor||||5||
Z||000000||David Gamache||01-11-2000||11:42 PM||||I understand some people have changed the crankshaft on the 2.8L motors to achieve a longer stroke much like a V-8 motor(placing a 400 crank in a 350 motor). Does anyone know which motor(3.?)and vehicle(s) the crank can be switched from to accomplish such a project? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||01-12-2000||02:20 AM||||Pretty much any 3.1 crank will fit large journal 2.8 engines.  New pistons are needed with the hole a third inch higher.  I had to grind off a piece of casting to clear a rod nut but otherwise it drops right in, just like a 383 stroker kit for small block chevy.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric||01-12-2000||03:20 PM||||Check the search function for 3.1, 3.2 , etc.  There is more information than you could possibly know what to do with.  Every question you have or will have we have already experienced and wrote about it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||la9||01-12-2000||08:21 PM||||Just an opinion but I am the middle of a rebuild and I would say the most cost effective plan would be to buy the 3.4L crate engine from GM. It won't be much more than a rebuild, plus you'll save a lot of time, and the engine will be new.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||01-12-2000||11:41 PM||||I am building a 3.1 for my 88 GT and am trying to do this on a minimal budget. I got the owner of the machine shop to find a rebuild kit with crank- approx $450. He is working a set of heads for me now. Most of the money will be spent on them. Intake valves opened to 1.78 and 1.5 exhaust with undercut stems and full porting. When more stuff starts to come together, I will post it here.||||reg||1
Z||000005||2FAST4U||01-13-2000||12:03 AM||||If i'm not mistaken yhe 3.4 crate motor from Chevy is for the S10 pickup and has the starter on the wrong side.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||01-13-2000||12:06 AM||||Check past threads about 3.4 block mods. Starter holes are not a problem.||||reg||1
